  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 4, ‘Share of countries by the number of indicators and sub-indicators for which data is available on the NHWA data platform’ (Source: WHO National Health Workforce Accounts, 2025). A 100% stacked horizontal bar chart across six categories (10 or less, 11 to 20, 21 to 30, 31 to 40, 41 to 50, and 51 or more indicators/sub-indicators) for Global, the six WHO regions (AFR, AMR, SEAR, EUR, EMR, WPR), and the four World Bank income groups (HIC, UMIC, LMIC, LIC). Globally, 4% of countries have data for 10 or fewer indicators/sub-indicators, 27% for 11 to 20, 21% for 21 to 30, 12% for 31 to 40, 27% for 41 to 50, and 9% for 51 or more.",
